{comment: Intro}
[D5]

{comment: Verse 1}
[D5]You were the Word at the beginning, one with God, the Lord most high
Your hidden glory in creation now revealed in You our Christ

{comment: Chorus 1}
[D]	              [A]
What a beautiful name it is, what a beautiful name it is
What a beautiful name it is, nothing compares to this
[Bm7]       [A]        [G]
The name of Jesus   Christ my King
What a beautiful name it is the name of Jesus

{comment: Verse 2}
[D]		                [G]          [Bm7]       [A]
You didnt heaven without us, so Jesus, You brought heaven down
[Bm7]	  [A/C#]                  [D]	       [G][Bm7]       [A]
My sin was great, Your love was greater. What could separate us now
Interlude    G (A - A - G - G)    A  (F# - F# - E - E)
{ci: 3x}
[Bm (A - A - G - G)  *D/F#  (F# - F# - C# - C#)]
*3rd time: A

{comment: Bridge 1 & 2}
[G]		 [A]
1. Death could not hold You, the veil tore before You
2. You have no rival You have no equal
[Bm7]             [D/F#]
1. You silenced the boast of sin and grave
2.         Now and forever, God, You reign
[G]                     [A]
1. The heavens are roaring the praise of Your glory
2.    Yours is the kingdom,	 Yours is the glory
[Bm7]  	[A]
1.      For You are raised to life again
2. Yours is the name above all names

{comment: Chorus 3}
{ci: same chords as Chorus 1}
{ci: Repeat Bridge 2 and Chorus 3; repeat last line of Chorus as desired; end on G}
